{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"const VueQueryPlugin: object;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/vue-query/src/vueQueryPlugin.ts#L75","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/vue-query/src/vueQueryPlugin.ts:75"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installs a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":" on the Vue app, making it available to every descendant component through\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":" — the Vue equivalent of React's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClientProvider"},{"type":"text","value":", but wired up as an app-level plugin\ninstead of a wrapping component."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-declaration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Declaration"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"install","children":[{"type":"text","value":"install"}]},{"type":"code","value":"install: (app: any, options: VueQueryPluginOptions) => void;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"app","children":[{"type":"text","value":"app"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/VueQueryPluginOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VueQueryPluginOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createApp } from 'vue'\nimport { VueQueryPlugin } from '@tanstack/vue-query'\n\nconst app = createApp(App)\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryClient"},{"type":"text","value":" you constructed yourself — useful for SSR, where you need a fresh "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":" per\nrequest, or when the same instance also needs to be used outside of Vue components:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { QueryClient, VueQueryPlugin } from '@tanstack/vue-query'\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin, { queryClient })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Or pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryClientConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" to let the plugin construct the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":" for you, with your own defaults:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"app.use(VueQueryPlugin, {\n  queryClientConfig: {\n    defaultOptions: { queries: { staleTime: 5 * 1000 } },\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"type-declaration","text":"Type Declaration","level":2},{"id":"install","text":"install","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"app","text":"app","level":5},{"id":"options","text":"options?","level":5},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nconst VueQueryPlugin: object;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/vue-query/src/vueQueryPlugin.ts:75](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/vue-query/src/vueQueryPlugin.ts#L75)\n\nInstalls a `QueryClient` on the Vue app, making it available to every descendant component through\n`useQueryClient` — the Vue equivalent of React's `QueryClientProvider`, but wired up as an app-level plugin\ninstead of a wrapping component.\n\n## Type Declaration\n\n### install\n\n```ts\ninstall: (app: any, options: VueQueryPluginOptions) => void;\n```\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### app\n\n`any`\n\n##### options?\n\n[`VueQueryPluginOptions`](../type-aliases/VueQueryPluginOptions.md) = `{}`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Examples\n\n```ts\nimport { createApp } from 'vue'\nimport { VueQueryPlugin } from '@tanstack/vue-query'\n\nconst app = createApp(App)\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin)\n```\n\nPass a `queryClient` you constructed yourself — useful for SSR, where you need a fresh `QueryClient` per\nrequest, or when the same instance also needs to be used outside of Vue components:\n```ts\nimport { QueryClient, VueQueryPlugin } from '@tanstack/vue-query'\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin, { queryClient })\n```\n\nOr pass `queryClientConfig` to let the plugin construct the `QueryClient` for you, with your own defaults:\n```ts\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin, {\n  queryClientConfig: {\n    defaultOptions: { queries: { staleTime: 5 * 1000 } },\n  },\n})\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: VueQueryPlugin\ntitle: VueQueryPlugin\n---\n\n```ts\nconst VueQueryPlugin: object;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/vue-query/src/vueQueryPlugin.ts:75](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/vue-query/src/vueQueryPlugin.ts#L75)\n\nInstalls a `QueryClient` on the Vue app, making it available to every descendant component through\n`useQueryClient` — the Vue equivalent of React's `QueryClientProvider`, but wired up as an app-level plugin\ninstead of a wrapping component.\n\n## Type Declaration\n\n### install\n\n```ts\ninstall: (app: any, options: VueQueryPluginOptions) => void;\n```\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### app\n\n`any`\n\n##### options?\n\n[`VueQueryPluginOptions`](../type-aliases/VueQueryPluginOptions.md) = `{}`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Examples\n\n```ts\nimport { createApp } from 'vue'\nimport { VueQueryPlugin } from '@tanstack/vue-query'\n\nconst app = createApp(App)\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin)\n```\n\nPass a `queryClient` you constructed yourself — useful for SSR, where you need a fresh `QueryClient` per\nrequest, or when the same instance also needs to be used outside of Vue components:\n```ts\nimport { QueryClient, VueQueryPlugin } from '@tanstack/vue-query'\n\nconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin, { queryClient })\n```\n\nOr pass `queryClientConfig` to let the plugin construct the `QueryClient` for you, with your own defaults:\n```ts\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin, {\n  queryClientConfig: {\n    defaultOptions: { queries: { staleTime: 5 * 1000 } },\n  },\n})\n```\n"}
